Chapter: LogLive
  cites Cvmm chapter LogViewer
  cites Kernel chapter AppLog
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts

 The view of the application log on the disk's fact store: one row per
 AppLog entry, oldest first, with AppLog's six levels (0 trace to 5 fatal)
 as the viewer's six severities and the writing app as the source.

Section: Mapping

  ll-severity : Integer -> LogSeverity
  ll-severity (level) =
    if level <= 0 then LogTrace
    else if level == 1 then LogDebug
    else if level == 2 then LogInfo
    else if level == 3 then LogWarn
    else if level == 4 then LogError
    else LogFatal

  ll-append : LogViewerState, List AppLogEntry, Integer, Integer -> LogViewerState
  ll-append (lv) (es) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then lv
    else let e = list-at es i
    in ll-append (lv-append lv (e.ale-timestamp) (SrcApp (e.ale-app)) (ll-severity (e.ale-level)) (e.ale-message)) es (i + 1) n

  lv-from-applog : List AppLogEntry -> LogViewerState
  lv-from-applog (es) = ll-append log-viewer-new es 0 (list-length es)

  lv-live : DiskFactStore -> LogViewerState
  lv-live (ds) = lv-from-applog (app-log-read ds)

